ool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/03/02/aercap-holdings-nv-aer-q4-2020-earnings-call-trans/"},{"c":"AER 2020 Q4","e":"aer","d":"2021-03-02","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Peter Juhas","x":"The cash accounting impact related primarily to airlines that are in restructuring or bankruptcy.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/03/02/aercap-holdings-nv-aer-q4-2020-earnings-call-trans/"},{"c":"AER 2020 Q4","e":"aer","d":"2021-03-02","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Peter Juhas","x":"So I think that the building blocks of that are, one, we've got a number of airlines that are still in restructuring, and those will come back online during the course of the year.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/03/02/aercap-holdings-nv-aer-q4-2020-earnings-call-trans/"},{"c":"AER 2021 Q1","e":"aer","d":"2021-04-28","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Peter Juhas","x":"LATAM is one of the airlines that's making progress on its restructuring and emergence from bankruptcy.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/04/28/aercap-holdings-nv-aer-q1-2021-earnings-call-trans/"},{"c":"AER 2021 Q1","e":"aer","d":"2021-04-28","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Peter Juhas","x":"So, that's going to be the biggest driver, the return of flight for most of those, because obviously those have mostly been airlines that are in bankruptcy or other restructuring, right.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/04/28/aercap-holdings-nv-aer-q1-2021-earnings-call-trans/"},{"c":"AER 2021 Q2","e":"aer","d":"2021-07-29","l":"cost_cuts","r":"analyst","s":"Vincent Caintic","x":"And then I think you've also had restructuring of some leases where maybe there's some variable aspect to it. but maybe if you could help us understand in how to forecast the portfolio lease rate going forward.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/07/29/aercap-holdings-nv-aer-q2-2021-earnings-call-trans/"},{"c":"AER 2021 Q3","e":"aer","d":"2021-11-10","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Peter Juhas","x":"Other leasing expenses were $54 million for the third quarter, an increase from $40 million in 2020 and the increase was mainly due to higher default and restructuring related costs during the quarter.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/11/10/aercap-holdings-nv-aer-q3-2021-earnings-call-trans/"},{"c":"AER 2021 Q3","e":"aer","d":"2021-11-10","l":"cost_cuts","r":"analyst","s":"Helane Becker","x":"…this and I just missed it and I apologize if you did, are you going to look and talk to the OEMs about potentially restructuring that order book or beyond 2024 since you're mostly placed through year-end 2023 or are you just going to go ahead and combine them and hope for the best so to speak.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/11/10/aercap-holdings-nv-aer-q3-2021-earnings-call-trans/"},{"c":"AER 2021 Q4","e":"aer","d":"2022-03-30","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Aengus Kelly","x":"Airlines in Europe benefit from higher average fuel hedging than their North American counterparts, and recent statements from the airlines suggest they are confident that they can pass through higher oil prices as yields remain strong.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2022/03/30/aercap-holdings-aer-q4-2021-earnings-call-transcri/"},{"c":"AER 2022 Q1","e":"aer","d":"2022-05-17","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Aengus Kelly","x":"Importantly, when I speak to airline CEOs, I hear a consistent message, which is that demand is strong enough in the US and Europe to pass through higher input costs.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2022/05/17/aercap-holdings-aer-q1-2022-earnings-call-transcri/"},{"c":"AER 2022 Q1","e":"aer","d":"2022-05-17","l":"pricing_power","r":"analyst","s":"Andrew Lobbenberg","x":"So to what extent do you have protection mechanisms that cap the price increases to the aircraft orders?","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2022/05/17/aercap-holdings-aer-q1-2022-earnings-call-transcri/"},{"c":"AER 2025 Q4","e":"aer","d":"2026-02-06","l":"ai_spend","r":"management","s":"Aengus Kelly","x":"That's not to say that we are—that doesn't mean that we're making some massive AI investment.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/02/06/aercap-aer-q4-2025-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"AER 2025 Q4","e":"aer","d":"2026-02-06","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Aengus Kelly","x":"The cargo market has shown tremendous resilience despite global trade tariffs and other geopolitical challenges.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/02/06/aercap-aer-q4-2025-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"AER 2025 Q4","e":"aer","d":"2026-02-06","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Peter Juhas","x":"Leasing expenses were higher than usual due to restructuring costs related to the Spirit Airlines bankruptcy.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/02/06/aercap-aer-q4-2025-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"AER 2025 Q4","e":"aer","d":"2026-02-06","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Peter Juhas","x":"This reflects the net impact of the Spirit restructuring as well as other unusual items and the timing of maintenance activity that I mentioned earlier.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/02/06/aercap-aer-q4-2025-earnings-call-transcript/"},{"c":"AER 2026 Q1","e":"aer","d":"2026-04-29","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Peter Juhas","x":"Leasing expenses were $110 million, which is a significant decrease from the fourth quarter when we recognized the majority of the restructuring costs related to the Spirit Airlines bankruptcy.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/05/04/aercap-aer-q1-2026-earnings-transcript/"},{"c":"AER 2026 Q2","e":"aer","d":"2026-07-29","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"Aengus Kelly","x":"Disciplined capital deployment and increa